3.What is the result of margin: 0 auto; on an inline element?
A)It centers the element
B)Nothing
C)It moves it to the top
D)It makes it block

✅ Correct Answer: B) Nothing

Simple English:

margin: 0 auto; does not work on an inline element.

It only works for block elements that have a width.

Example:
span {
  margin: 0 auto;
}

👉 span is an inline element, so nothing happens.

Easy Remember:
✅ Block element (div) + margin: 0 auto; = Center
❌ Inline element (span) + margin: 0 auto; = Nothing
Options:
❌ A) It centers the element
✅ B) Nothing
❌ C) It moves it to the top
❌ D) It makes it block

✅ Final Answer: B) Nothing


4.Which property is used to set the space between the border and the outline?
A)outline-margin 
B )outline-offset 
C )border-outline-gap 
D )outline-padding

Simple English:

outline-offset is used to add space between the border and the outline.

Example:
.box {
  border: 2px solid black;
  outline: 2px solid red;
  outline-offset: 5px;
}

👉 The red outline will be 5px away from the border.

Easy Remember:
outline = Outside the border
outline-offset = Space between border and outline
