9.Does box-shadow increase the actual width of the element in the layout?

A)Yes
B)No /// answers
C)Only if inset
D)Only in Firefox

Simple English:

box-shadow does NOT increase the actual width or height of an element.

It only adds a shadow outside the element. The shadow is visual only and does not affect the page layout.

Example:
.box {
  width: 200px;
  height: 100px;
  box-shadow: 5px 5px 10px gray;
}

👉 The box is still 200px wide.
The shadow appears outside, but the element's size does not change.

Easy Remember:
Border → Can affect the box size.
Box-shadow → Only a visual effect, does not change the layout.
Options:
❌ A) Yes
✅ B) No
❌ C) Only if inset
❌ D) Only in Firefox

✅ Final Answer: B) No


